hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27988","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us: Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Yazid narrated to us, his father informed him, he said: I stayed with Umm Ayyub, with whom the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stayed; I stayed with her, and she narrated to me this from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: That they prepared food containing some of these greens, and brought it near, and he disliked it, and said to his companions: Eat, for I am not as one of you; I fear to harm my companion, meaning the angel."
"27989","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah, from his father, from Umm Ayyub, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The Quran was revealed upon seven letters; whichever you recite suffices you."
"28174","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid narrated to us, his father informed him, he said: I stayed with Umm Ayyub, those with whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed, I stayed with her and she narrated to me this on the authority of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): They burdened themselves with food containing some of these greens, and they brought it near, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked it and said to his companions: Eat, I am not as one of you, I fear to harm my companion, meaning the angel."
"28175","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaydullah meaning Ibn Abi Yazid, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Umm Ayyub, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Quran was sent down upon seven letters, whichever you recite suffices you."
